# requirements.in -- the container's declared Python stack.
#
# This file is the declaration: the general-purpose scientific stack the agent
# is told it has (AGENTS.md § Environment). `requirements.lock` beside it is the
# resolution -- every transitive dependency pinned, with hashes -- and it is what
# the image installs. Never edit the lock by hand; regenerate it:
#
#   uv pip compile --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu \
#       --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes \
#       requirements.in -o requirements.lock
#
# The lock is platform-specific by construction (`--python-platform`), which is
# right here: the image is linux/amd64 only, and a single-platform resolution
# avoids marker-gated alternates that would never be installed.
#
# Against an existing lock, uv keeps the versions already pinned there wherever
# they still satisfy this file and resolves only what changed -- so editing one
# line here moves one package, not the whole stack. Add `--upgrade` to move
# everything to current, or delete the lock first for a clean resolution.
#
# What is deliberately NOT here: any package that operationalises one field's
# methods. The venv is writable and egress is open, so the agent installs what
# its question needs and logs the install (AGENTS.md); the harness supplies the
# substrate, not the method. Adding a package here is a promise to the agent --
# keep this list and AGENTS.md's description of the environment in agreement.
#
# Versions float to whatever the lock resolves on the day it is regenerated,
# with one exception below. The lock is the pin; this file is the intent.

# --- Core scientific stack ------------------------------------------------------
# pandas is held at 2.3.x deliberately: pandas 3 makes copy-on-write the default
# and changes string dtypes, so the idioms these models have memorised start
# warning or erroring mid-run. numpy and scipy float to whatever pandas and the
# rest agree on; the lock records the exact versions.
numpy
pandas==2.3.*
scipy
statsmodels
scikit-learn

# --- Plotting ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# MPLBACKEND=Agg is set in the image, so matplotlib never looks for a display.
matplotlib
seaborn

# --- Columnar and file IO -----------------------------------------------------------
# openpyxl because pandas cannot open an .xlsx without it, and a run that finds
# that out at the first spreadsheet loses an hour to a one-line install.
pyarrow
polars
duckdb
openpyxl

# --- Web access and browser automation --------------------------------------------
# Egress is open, so the agent fetches its own data and literature. `playwright`
# drives headless Chromium for web UIs and portals a scripted fetch cannot reach;
# the browser binary itself is installed in the Dockerfile, not here. `httpx` and
# `tenacity` are the fetch-and-retry pair; beautifulsoup4/lxml parse what comes
# back; pypdf reads PDFs the agent downloads.
requests
httpx
tenacity
beautifulsoup4
lxml
playwright
pypdf

# --- Working tools --------------------------------------------------------------------
tqdm
pytest
